WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:06.900
Get ready for killers to be reborn and for your&nbsp;
childhood memories turn into nightmares, as 2023's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:12.684
blend of horror sequels, reboots, and originals&nbsp;
are poised to blow gore-hungry audiences away!

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:18.720
The first horror movie coming out in 2023&nbsp;
is M3GAN, which is set to arrive on January&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:23.880
6 from director Gerard Johnstone and&nbsp;
writers James Wan and Akela Cooper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:28.740
as well as producer Jason Blum. Wan and Cooper&nbsp;
previously worked together on Malignant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.240
while this is the second feature from&nbsp;
Johnstone, who directed Housebound in 2014.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:38.640
M3GAN also marks Allison Williams' return to the&nbsp;
horror spotlight after her chilling performance in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:44.700
Get Out in 2017. The premise is refreshing&nbsp;
but familiar, as roboticist Gemma utilizes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:49.500
her knowledge of artificial intelligence to&nbsp;
build a lifelike doll. It's reminiscent of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.780
the Child's Play remake from 2019, but MEGAN&nbsp;
dares to shake things up by giving audiences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:59.820
a passionate depiction of survival between two&nbsp;
people who deeply need each other. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:04.620
Gemma deciding to use her M3GAN prototype to help&nbsp;
take care of her recently orphaned niece doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:10.140
go well, and the result looks to be a palpable&nbsp;
tale of technology vs. humans with horror tricks.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.045
"I won't let anything harm you."

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:17.400
The prospects of a new Evil Dead movie have been&nbsp;
in the works since Fede Alvarez directed a soft&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:22.620
reboot back in 2013. Even before then, there'd&nbsp;
been rumblings about a new film for years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:26.580
with Bruce Campbell set to reprise&nbsp;
his role as Ash Williams. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:32.640
the 2013 edition was billed as a "reimagining" of&nbsp;
the 1981 original, with Ash absent from the story.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:36.720
Instead, the reboot focused on new&nbsp;
characters attempting to survive in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:40.620
a cabin while supernatural monsters&nbsp;
seek to possess and kill them. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:43.800
Lee Cronin has taken on the task&nbsp;
of directing a fifth installment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:49.380
called Evil Dead Rise. The plot follows two&nbsp;
sisters, Ellie and Beth, who must fight against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:54.000
flesh-hungry demons living in the deep pits&nbsp;
below Ellie's Los Angeles apartment building.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.960
What makes the Evil Dead franchise so&nbsp;
refreshing is how it always aims to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:02.040
reinvent itself. The 2013 version&nbsp;
proved itself a worthy entry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:06.402
so expectations for Evil Dead Rise&nbsp;
are high ahead of its April release.

00:02:07.134 --> 00:02:12.120
Scream VI is scheduled to hit theaters on&nbsp;
March 10, with the story continuing right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:17.940
where it left off in 2022's Scream, as sisters&nbsp;
Sam and Tara and twins Mindy and Chad are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:21.960
attempting to put their lives back together&nbsp;
as they leave Woodsboro for New York City.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:26.940
Scream VI has garnered a lot of attention&nbsp;
in recent months, specifically because of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:32.100
Neve Campbell declining to reprise her role as&nbsp;
Sidney Prescott due to a failure to agree on a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:37.080
new contract. It's hard to imagine a Scream movie&nbsp;
without Campbell, but we'll see what the new faces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:42.540
have to offer and how fellow longtime cast member&nbsp;
Courteney Cox carries the franchise's legacy.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:48.000
Cox doesn't have to do it alone, though, as she'll&nbsp;
be joined by the returning Jenna Ortega as Tara,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:52.800
as well as series newcomer Samara Weaving.&nbsp;
This also marks the first film in the franchise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:57.960
without David Arquette, whose character Dewey --&nbsp;
spoiler alert! -- died in the last installment.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:00.000
"It's an honor."

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:05.520
By the time Insidious: Fear the Dark hits theaters&nbsp;
in July, it'll have been almost five years since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:10.920
Insidious: The Last Key graced our screens.&nbsp;
Franchise regulars Patrick Wilson, Rose Byrne,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:15.900
and Ty Simpkins are all set to reprise their roles&nbsp;
as the Lambert family for the first time since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:23.040
Chapter 2 in 2013. And Wilson is also set to make&nbsp;
his directorial debut with this new entry. Series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:28.380
creator Leigh Whannell is also back, with a "story&nbsp;
by" credit and also as one of the producers.

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:32.880
Fear the Dark is set to continue the Lamberts'&nbsp;
story, as Dalton is headed to college,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:37.860
with the Lipstick-Face Demon returning to&nbsp;
bring his and his dad Josh's past into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:40.800
present. The last two installments&nbsp;
earned less-than-stellar reviews,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:44.760
so here's to hoping that this go-round&nbsp;
can get the franchise back on track.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:50.580
The Haunted Mansion that's set to arrive in&nbsp;
theaters on August 11 is neither a remake nor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:54.420
a sequel to The Haunted Mansion&nbsp;
that came out in 2003. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:57.960
it's another, separate adaptation&nbsp;
of Disney's classic theme park ride.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.720
This updated version boasts a star-studded cast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:06.420
with Rosario Dawson, LaKeith Stanfield,&nbsp;
Owen Wilson, Winona Ryder, Danny DeVito,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:12.060
Jamie Lee Curtis, Tiffany Haddish, Jared&nbsp;
Leto, and Dan Levy all on the call sheet.

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:15.780
The story focuses on Dawson as&nbsp;
single mom Gabbie and her young son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:19.800
who are hoping for a fresh start in life&nbsp;
when they move into a New Orleans mansion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:24.360
that's possessed. And with Justin Simien,&nbsp;
who directed Dear White People and Bad Hair,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:28.467
at the helm, the sky's the limit for&nbsp;
this new take on a Disneyland classic.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:33.000
Five years after the release of The Nun,&nbsp;
James Wan is back with another installment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:37.020
in this Conjuring spinoff series, as he&nbsp;
co-writes the story with Akela Cooper.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:42.000
With director Michael Chaves at the helm, The&nbsp;
Nun 2 serves as a prequel to The Conjuring 2,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:46.260
as it continues to explore the demonic&nbsp;
secrets of the paranormal entity Valak.

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:51.120
Taissa Farmiga returns as Sister Irene,&nbsp;
who is once again tasked with battling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:54.780
Valak. Farmiga shined in her first&nbsp;
outing in the Conjuring franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:58.260
rivaling the work of her older&nbsp;
sister Vera as Lorraine Warren.

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:04.200
The Nun struggled to please critics, but&nbsp;
it made heaps of cash, raking in over $365&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:09.780
million at the box office. But a solid script&nbsp;
could certainly deliver plenty of unforgettable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:14.244
frights this time around, so let's all plan&nbsp;
to get back in the habit come September.

00:05:14.244 --> 00:05:15.144
"Amen."

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:21.120
There are some movies that are so legendary that&nbsp;
they can never be remade, and 1973's The Exorcist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:26.760
certainly appears to be one of them. Luckily,&nbsp;
David Gordon Green's 2023 Exorcist film, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:31.980
is currently untitled, is meant to act as a direct&nbsp;
sequel to the original, as opposed to a reboot.

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:36.840
Set to hit theaters in October, the 2023&nbsp;
Exorcist is more than likely not going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:42.180
to garner quite the success its predecessor&nbsp;
enjoyed 50 years ago. But writers Scott Teems,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:46.740
Danny McBride, Peter Sattler, and Green are&nbsp;
all primed to approach this new installment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:52.200
in a similar fashion as the Halloween trilogy&nbsp;
that concluded in 2022. The film will eliminate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:55.560
all other storylines that have occurred&nbsp;
within the franchise since the original.

00:05:55.560 --> 00:06:00.300
The divisiveness of 2022's Halloween Ends&nbsp;
may not bode well for Green and company,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:05.400
but it will be interesting to see what direction&nbsp;
they take nevertheless. With Leslie Odom Jr,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:10.140
Ann Dowd, and original Exorcist star&nbsp;
Ellen Burstyn all set to play key roles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:14.634
2023's Exorcist will do its best&nbsp;
to possess audiences once again.

00:06:14.634 --> 00:06:15.894
"Is she gonna die?"

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:22.680
"No."

00:06:22.946 --> 00:06:27.120
Saw has been a pillar in the horror&nbsp;
genre since its inception in 2004,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:30.840
and every subsequent installment,&nbsp;
no matter how silly or illogical,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:34.500
has brought something to the table&nbsp;
to satisfy its devoted fanbase.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:40.140
The 2021 Saw spinoff Spiral found modest&nbsp;
box office success, and it felt inevitable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:44.160
that a direct sequel would arrive, but&nbsp;
that part of the universe now appears to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:48.240
be on the backburner. What Bell's return&nbsp;
to the franchise means exactly for Saw X&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:54.180
remains to be seen. John Kramer was supposedly&nbsp;
killed off at the end of 2006's Saw III , but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:58.260
Bell has returned in various flashbacks&nbsp;
and dream sequences in the years since.

00:06:58.260 --> 00:07:03.840
Even though 2017's Jigsaw, the last Saw film&nbsp;
with Bell, wasn't exactly well-loved by critics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:08.400
it managed to make its budget back ten&nbsp;
times over. Box office success in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:12.000
face of critical derision has remained&nbsp;
a consistency within the franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:15.540
so Saw X should be expected&nbsp;
to maintain the status quo.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:20.220
Not too many upcoming horror movies have as&nbsp;
much buzz as Winnie-the-Pooh: Blood and Honey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:25.200
a grisly and gory take on the beloved children's&nbsp;
book character. Winnie-the-Pooh became public&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:30.360
domain in 2022, and with Disney no longer holding&nbsp;
the exclusive rights to the source material,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:35.460
writer-director Rhys Frake-Waterfield set out&nbsp;
to turn a beloved cartoon into a nightmare.

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:39.660
The premise of Blood and Honey follows&nbsp;
anthropomorphic versions of Pooh and Piglet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:44.700
descending into madness after Christopher Robin&nbsp;
goes off to college. The two woodland creatures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:49.560
kill and eat Eeyore and attempt to wreak havoc&nbsp;
on humans after learning that Christopher is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:54.060
now married. Naturally enough, this includes&nbsp;
attacking a cabin full of sorority girls.

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:58.980
Blood and Honey initially garnered attention&nbsp;
after a teaser was released in May 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:04.440
and horror fans and Disney adults alike should be&nbsp;
drawn to this reimagining. It's set to be released&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:09.240
on February 15 as an exclusive event through its&nbsp;
distribution company, Altitude Film. Whatever your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:13.935
expectations regarding quality, Blood and Honey&nbsp;
should be worth seeing for the shock factor alone.

00:08:13.935 --> 00:08:16.401
"Oh, bother."

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:21.120
The last Stephen King book to become a&nbsp;
film was the 2022 remake of Firestarter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:25.860
which was widely panned by critics. Hoping to&nbsp;
get the cinematic world of King back on track,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:30.720
Rob Savage is helming The Boogeyman,&nbsp;
based on King's 1978 short story of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:34.020
the same name that appeared in the&nbsp;
author's collection Night Shift.

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:38.460
If it stays true to its source material, The&nbsp;
Boogeyman should follow two sisters who are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:41.820
haunted by a sadistic, paranormal&nbsp;
monster while grieving the death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:46.080
of their mother. This is one of King's&nbsp;
lesser-known short stories, so Savage and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:50.340
company have a promising opportunity to bring&nbsp;
prominence to an otherwise overlooked tale.

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:55.320
The Boogeyman is not set for a theatrical release,&nbsp;
as it's due instead for exclusive streaming on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.320 --> 00:09:01.440
Hulu sometime in 2023. With a budding young cast&nbsp;
that includes Madison Hu and Sophie Thatcher, as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:06.240
well as a script from A Quiet Place's Scott Beck&nbsp;
and Bryan Woods, the promise is certainly there.

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:11.340
Adapting Paul G. Tremblay's 2018 novel&nbsp;
The Cabin at the End of the World,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:13.380
M. Night Shyamalan is back&nbsp;
with Knock at the Cabin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:17.340
an apocalyptic psychological horror&nbsp;
film set to hit theaters in February.

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:22.380
The story of Knock at the Cabin follows a family&nbsp;
of three who are taken hostage by four friends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:27.840
with a lot of demands as the world is about to&nbsp;
end. Tremblay's book is emotional, cutthroat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:32.760
and merciless. How Shyamalan will translate that&nbsp;
to the big screen is something to look forward to.

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:37.620
The book also offers a lot of commentary on&nbsp;
modern-day homophobia, so it'll be interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:42.840
to see how that plays out in the adaptation.&nbsp;
Overall, it's a story about paranoia, enduring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:47.460
love, and survival in the wake of disaster&nbsp;
and sacrifice. Many of the ideas at play in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:52.140
Knock at the Cabin have been touched on before&nbsp;
in other horror flicks, such as The Strangers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:56.868
and The Purge, but the apocalyptic element&nbsp;
should hopefully offer a breath of fresh air.

00:09:56.868 --> 00:10:02.028
"The four of us are here&nbsp;
to prevent the apocalypse."

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:08.280
Ti West and Mia Goth had an incredible 2022&nbsp;
together. After releasing X in March, it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:13.140
quickly revealed via an after-credits teaser that&nbsp;
West had also shot a prequel at the same time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:18.900
That follow-up, Pearl, dazzled audiences even more&nbsp;
than X, and when it hit theaters in September,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:23.760
it was then confirmed that a final film&nbsp;
would arrive in 2023 to make it a trilogy.

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:28.680
At the heart of the trilogy are two characters&nbsp;
played by Goth. X introduced the elderly Pearl,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:33.180
who yearns for her lost vibrancy, and the&nbsp;
young Maxine, a porn star and the daughter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:37.680
of a fundamentalist Christian preacher. While&nbsp;
Pearl follows the origins of the antagonist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:42.900
who kills all of Maxine's friends in 1979,&nbsp;
MaXXXine will pick up after the events of X&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.900 --> 00:10:48.660
to focus entirely on the title character. With&nbsp;
a 1980s setting, West is certain to deliver a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:53.820
stylish time capsule of Reagan-era nostalgia&nbsp;
and another memorable performance out of Goth.

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:58.080
A release date for MaXXXine hasn't been made&nbsp;
official yet, and a more detailed premise is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:02.460
being kept under lock and key. All we have&nbsp;
to hold us over for now is a short title&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.460 --> 00:11:06.120
card teaser that ran at the end of Pearl.&nbsp;
Though the script is still in development,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:10.140
the fact that West was able to churn out&nbsp;
X and Pearl within mere months of each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:15.600
other suggests that we can probably expect to&nbsp;
see MaXXXine hit theaters before 2023 ends.

